193452745"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-d9625b0c-547f-4c19-be69-d5360b8e8806"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Overview of T and D-T results in JET with ITER-like wall","type":"Journal Review","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-776144","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Within the 9th European Framework programme, since 2021 EUROfusion is operating five tokamaks under the auspices of a single Task Force called ‘Tokamak Exploitation’. The goal is to benefit from the complementary capabilities of each machine in a coordinated way and help in developing a scientific output scalable to future largre machines. The programme of this Task Force ensures that ASDEX Upgrade, MAST-U, TCV, WEST and JET (since 2022) work together to achieve the objectives of Missions 1 and 2 of the EUROfusion Roadmap: i) demonstrate plasma scenarios that increase the success margin of ITER and satisfy the requirements of DEMO and, ii) demonstrate an integrated approach that can handle the large power leaving ITER and DEMO plasmas. The Tokamak Exploitation task force has therefore organized experiments on these two missions with the goal to strengthen the physics and operational basis for the ITER baseline scenario and for exploiting the recent plasma exhaust enhancements in all four devices (PEX: Plasma EXhaust) for exploring the solution for handling heat and particle exhaust in ITER and develop the conceptual solutions for DEMO. The ITER Baseline scenario has been developed in a similar way in ASDEX Upgrade, TCV and JET. Key risks for ITER such as disruptions and run-aways have been also investigated in TCV, ASDEX Upgrade and JET. Experiments have explored successfully different divertor configurations (standard, super-X, snowflakes) in MAST-U and TCV and studied tungsten melting in WEST and ASDEX Upgrade. The input from the smaller devices to JET has also been proven successful to set-up novel control schemes on disruption avoidance and detachment.","author_count":50,"contributors":["Joffrin, E.","Wischmeier, M.","Baruzzo, M.","Hakola, A.","Kappatou, A.","Keeling, D.","Labit, B.","Tsitrone, E.","Vianello, N.","Abate, D.","Adamek, J.","Agostini, M.","Albert, C.","Devasagayam, F. C.P.Albert","Aleiferis, S.","Alessi, E.","Alhage, J.","Allan, S.","Allcock, J.","Alonzo, M.","Anastasiou, G.","Sunden, E. Andersson","Angioni, C.","Anquetin, Y.","Appel, L.","Apruzzese, G. M.","Ariola, M.","Arnas, C.","Artaud, J. F.","Gerru, R.","Jacobsen, Asger Schou","Järleblad, H.","Jensen, T.","Klinkby, Esben Bryndt","Korsholm, Søren Bang","Rud, M.","Nem, R. D.","Nielsen, Anders Henry","Nielsen, Stefan Kragh","Poulsen, A.","Ragona, R.","Rasmussen, J.","Reman, B. C.G.","Salewski, Mirko","Senstius, M. G.","Schmidt, B.S.","Thrysøe, Alexander Simon","Valentini, A.","Verdier, T.","Wiesenberger, M."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-789113"],"filters":{"added":"2025-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corpau":["JET Contributorsb, the MAST-U Teamc, the TCV Teamd, the WEST Teame, the EUROfusion Tokamak Exploitation Team"],"corresponding_author":["Joffrin, E."],"country":["Austria","Belgium","Czechia","Finland","France","Germany","Greece","Italy","Sweden","Switzerland","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["Aalto University","Agenzia nazionale per le nuove tecnologie, l'energia e lo sviluppo economico sostenibile","All Global Affiliations","CNRS","CREATE Consortium","Czech Academy of Sciences","Ghent University","Graz University of Technology","Max Planck Institute for Plasma Physics","National Research Council of Italy","National Technical University of Athens","Swiss Federal Institute of Technology Lausanne","United Kingdom Atomic Energy Authority","University of Padua","Uppsala University","VTT Technical Research Centre of Finland Ltd."],"keyword":["ASDEX Upgrade","EUROfusion","JET","TCV","WEST"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"overview of the eurofusion tokamak exploitation programme in support of iter and demo","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"djr","type-gr